{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence","id":1015604,"title":"Teleportation and Coincidence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-11T01:54:31-08:00","id":1015604,"title":"Teleportation and Coincidence","content":"I tend to assume that teleportation of yourself or another person can't be done Coincidentally outside the Umbra and Sanctums and the like. Moving an object from one concealed location to another would be Coincidental under HAP, but the idea that someone could step into a walk-in closet in Toronto and Coincidentally come out of a walk-in closet in Rio de Jinero never seemed right to me. I think I've figured out why. When I think of a Hypothetical Average Observer observing a teleporting mage, I don't think of them just being in the departure point and arrival point--I think of the Observer as going along for the ride. And as soon as they step out of the closet and into a setting where the buildings are different, it's going to be obvious that something unnatural happened. Even if you say the HAP is only in one location, an ACTUAL observer observed themself teleporting.<br /> <br /> This leaves the possibility of Coincidental teleportation to areas built to look identical, as long as the traveler stays confined to these areas until they go back to their original location. This could facilitate in-person interaction of mages from around the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T02:30:14-08:00","id":1015618,"title":"","content":"I personally am more flexible with what is coincidental and what is not. I imagine the HAO being in the &quot;room&quot;. Therefore, in you exemple, it would be vulgar only if the oberver opens the closet and finds out that the Mage vanished and there is obviously no way that is was a setup with a trapdoor or the like. That way, teleporting is often vulgar, but not always.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T02:56:20-08:00","id":1015622,"title":"","content":"The way How Do You Do That? handles the matter of teleportation is that when it says &quot;Hypothetical Average Observer&quot;, it means a hypothetical average human being who is in the room. For this reason, it states that so long as the HAO can't see the Mage wink out of existence, and there's a reasonable chance they could have left the area through mundane means, it's coincidental. Darkness and thick smoke or fog are very useful in the former regard, and a room simply having a window or other door (or corners one could duck around in the case of more open areas) can apply to the latter.<br /> <br /> For instance, I'm trying to escape some punks, and I duck into a nightclub bathroom. There's a window in the back large enough for a human to exit through, so I flip the lights off and do my thing. The punks storm in, someone turns the lights back on, and then they spend a few futile seconds scouring the area for my missing ass. No one saw me disappear, and it's entirely possible I effected my escape through the window. Coincidental. It would be even easier if it were in the dead of night, outside, where I could run off into the darkness and, for all intents and purposes, give any pursuers the slip.<br /> <br /> This is also why Mages would benefit from smoke grenades. They aren't nearly as loud as frag grenades, and they provide plenty of cover for a magickal getaway. Flashbangs too, given the bright flash and deafening sound. By the time any Hypothetical Average Observer rubbed sight back into their eyes, the Mage would be long gone, even if they &quot;walked right past them&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T03:18:11-08:00","id":1015627,"title":"","content":"It could be because I'm all about revised, but teleportation has always been vulgar from my standpoint. It's not just the HAO from the left location, but the HAO from the arrived location that needs to be considered. People don't just wink out or into existence or apear halfway around the world.<br /> <br /> The only exception might be in situations where teleportation is expected such as in a magic show, and then it would need to be from within the confinds of the stage.<br /> <br /> I'd say all that obscuring the magic does is turn it from vulgar with whiteness to vulgar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T09:19:04-08:00","id":1015695,"title":"","content":"I am so torn between what Saikou says and what Bluecho says. I think I've always defaulted to Saikou's way to do it, but, if the circumstances are just right, as per Bluecho, I think that kind of cleverness should be rewarded. And if the mage/player in question is clever in setting the situation up so they have that option.... Even more kudos.<br /> <br /> The one part in this that I would seriously have to take into account is the Focus as well. Some Foci seem like they might be more likely to draw the attention of witnesses than others. But, geeze, if the Hermetic had planned the bathroom as his exit point, inscribed the transportation circle on the floor (or the wall? as graffiti?) in advance, has a smoke grenade or turns off the lights, there are logical exit points and shows up in his locked and sealed apartment that he shares with his cat..... I still want it to be vulgar without witnesses.... but, but, but....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T09:39:21-08:00","id":1015702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1015695#post1015695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am so torn between what Saikou says and what Bluecho says. I think I've always defaulted to Saikou's way to do it, but, if the circumstances are just right, as per Bluecho, I think that kind of cleverness should be rewarded. And if the mage/player in question is clever in setting the situation up so they have that option.... Even more kudos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cleverly pulling of teleportation in a coicidental way is appropriately named &quot;The Batman&quot; in HDYDT ;p","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T13:10:06-08:00","id":1015799,"title":"","content":"The problem is the very concept of HAO. It is extremely vague, and worse, it doesn't make a lot of sense. It does make sense that an actual observer causes Paradox, meaning that Paradox comes from defying Consensus. It does make sense that a certain degree of &quot;Reality Bending&quot; causes Paradox without an observer, meaning that Paradox comes from defying local Pattern. It does make sense that pulling a trick the Mage proper fear being observed causes Paradox, meaning that Paradox comes from the very anxiety of the Mage.<br /> <br /> But HAO doesn't make a lot of sense. It isn't dependent on any, absolutely any IC quality, but on the very fact that the game is a game. The only measure of a HAO is the OoC observation of the scene. How does it fits with Mage? It would be interesting to see a game that works on such terms, or a given Mage's Paradigm working on such terms. But Mage doesn't seem to me a game that calls for that kind of meta-narrative by default, except on the rules for Paradox alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T13:41:30-08:00","id":1015811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1015702#post1015702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cleverly pulling of teleportation in a coicidental way is appropriately named &quot;The Batman&quot; in HDYDT ;p</div> </div> </div> </div>But... like most of the interesting or useful stuff in HDYDT, it's lost in a sea of tripe and offal (mostly floating masses of rancid Sphere-bloat).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T15:23:03-08:00","id":1015867,"title":"","content":"Two examples as food for thought.<br /> <br /> Think of the Professor's &quot;Transported Man&quot; trick from The Prestige. Two doors in their frames, facing the audience, maybe 10 feet apart. He bounces a ball and steps back through one door, and emerges from the other door in time to catch the ball. Let's set aside how it's accomplished in the movie (as it is half of the major reveal at the end) and assume he's some sort of mage and is using Correspondence 3. Is it coincidental? The audience is expecting to see unbelievable things. It's possible he's doing some mundane stagecraft. I'd argue it should be coincidental, but that says more about how much I prioritize setting and expectations of the witnesses when making that decision.<br /> <br /> From Dark Ages: Mage, the Ahl-I-Batin have set up many-pillared rooms in several major centers of Islamic power through the world (I always imagine Dwarrowdelf from LOTR). If you walk a very careful path through the pillars, you will emerge from the counterpart in another city - for example, from Baghdad to Cordoba). In game effects this is a permanent Correspondence - no wait, Al-Hajj 4 effect. Is this effective multiportal coincidental? I'd say yes, because the room is complicated enough that no HAP could be sure the mage wasn't already there when in fact he was just in another city. But I'm guessing most people will disagree with me here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7356,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","user":"haldir2012","date":".  Can't remember my Islamic centers of power 12-11-2016, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T20:46:58-08:00","id":1015968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1015867#post1015867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this effective multiportal coincidental? I'd say yes, because the room is complicated enough that no HAP could be sure the mage wasn't already there when in fact he was just in another city. But I'm guessing most people will disagree with me here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would tend to agree with you. It's pretty similar to the idea I had in the second paragraph. Within DA it's moot from a metaphysical standpoint because there's no distinction between overt and covert magic--but I think a modern version would still be Coincidental. The question is what happens when you step outside the building into a city where the people may not even speak your language. I think that would become retroactively Vulgar, and since there is no rule that I'm aware of for retroactively Vulgar Effects, I'd probably just give the player two Paradox. Why two? To make up for the fact that they got away with a Coincidental difficulty on their Arete roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T00:03:37-08:00","id":1016008,"title":"","content":"I tend to disagree with you. Especially nowadays, people travel to many places and you often meet someone who does not speak your native language. No problem with that. Concerning the retroactive paradox, there are none in my games. Mages get paradox when they toy with the fabric of reality if they go too obviously far or fail. But when the effect is done, it's done. Now, you can either use the disbelief effect to manage that, or make it part of your scenario to annoy the player (the technocrats found out about the effect, etc.)<br /> <br /> If you want to invoke some bygone in the center of Manhattan, you do not get paradox each time someone sees it. At the most you get one point when you perform the ritual if you succeed. However, prepare to deal with the consequences...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T00:48:45-08:00","id":1016020,"title":"","content":"While I don't particularly like the existence of the trait (it shouldn't be it's own trait because that replaces being clever), this is why we have Blatancy. The whole point of Blatancy is your character's skill at doing magic in front of people without stoking their disbelief.<br /> <br /> Most mages would find teleportation vulgar, because the HAO would be smart enough to realize there's no way for them to do that. Mages skilled in stage-craft and props can reverse it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T03:16:42-08:00","id":1016044,"title":"","content":"If the HAO is guarding the room where the mage teleported from, if there are no other exists that the mage could possible take (as in a walk in closet) i agree that it would be Vulgar. If there is a possibility (however slight) that the mage could escape from the room without magic it's Coincidental. Same goes for the &quot;landing zone&quot;, if there is no way the mage could get into the place without the HAO noticing it it's vulgar, if there's a possibility that he could have gone there by mundane means it's coincidental. As always it's up to the storyteller.<br /> And ofc it's Vulgar (with Witnesses) if the mage just pops out in an open space (Ally, conference room, town square).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T09:27:37-08:00","id":1016137,"title":"","content":"It's so subjective it's hard to make those calls though. <br /> <br /> To step outside of Teleportation, since that seems to be the usual kludge for coincidental vs. vulgar, here's a situation from our game last night.<br /> <br /> Our Hermetic was walking willingly into a Syndicate stronghold (because, you see, it was run by his long lost relatives and they asked nicely....) The group had the whatever-he-is-now technomancer (started off as a VA but a Technocratic Union VA from the 40s.... he's either becoming a Marauder or a Son of Ether at this point) give the Hermetic a souped-up ear bud. When he crossed the threshold, it went dead (of course), so the VA/SoE immediately started using his technomancy to reconfigure the ear bud at a distance (so that it used ultra-spacial gravo-metric gradients to carry the signal... or some such nonsense). <br /> <br /> So.... I had to make a call... coincidental or vulgar? The VA/SoE stated that he was physically changing the ear-bud from a machine that worked one way to one that worked another. I ended up deciding it was vulgar with no Sleeper Witnesses because it was in the Hermetic's ear. The Hermetic felt the ear bud get warm, buzz and wriggle around a little. <br /> <br /> But what if the Hermetic hadn't been wearing it? He took it out a few minutes later at the polite request of the Syndicate goon... I mean security guard (since they had detected the VA/SoE's manipulations... they didn't know what had happened, just that something had). What if it had changed when no one was touching it and no one had any reason to assume it wasn't a normal ear bud? Since there's no retroactive Paradox, if it looked like a normal earbud how would they ever know it was different if they didn't use it or take a look to see if it was made differently? (And what if they didn't have the Technology to know what ear bud innards are supposed to look like?) It allowed for two-way communication using bone conduction as well,,, but you can't SEE that it can do that) <br /> <br /> Later on he reconfigured it again, so he could project his voice through it at normal volume. (Sorta a tragic thing where he wanted to talk to his long lost mother, with whom the Hermetic was conversing.... since she was also the Hermetic's long lost daughter.... it's a chronicle fraught with a lot of complicated family relationships... and time travel.) Was it the sound projection from an &quot;ear bud&quot; that was vulgar? Or was it having a machine reconfigure itself at a distance so that it could do that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T12:46:33-08:00","id":1016199,"title":"","content":"HDYDT so commonly gives bad advice. I'm not saying the Batman wouldn't work, but you really have to take everything that book says with a grain of salt. The whole thing about not being seen is questionable.<br /> <br /> The thing is, even in HAP you usually can't hide from the hypothetical observer. There are ways but they usually feel like they are pushing the edges of the allowable. If there is a vantage point one can reasonably sit and say WTF from, it is Vulgar W/O Witnesses. So he question isn't how do you hide yourself from the Hypothetical Observer, it is how do you make every potential Hypothetical Observer think something normal happened? <br /> <br /> People get disoriented with sudden light changes, so you change the lights. People lose track of each other in a crowd, so you run into a crowd. If an observer could reasonably believe that he just lost sight of you in that instant, congrats, you've reached coincidental for the departure. If an observer could reasonably believe he just hadn't noticed you before, congrats, you've reached coincidental for the arrival.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T12:56:27-08:00","id":1016204,"title":"","content":"I was wondering. What about big tech-machinery stuff ? Imean the huge teleportation device. Could the Observer be satisfied by technology enabling teleportation ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T13:04:40-08:00","id":1016212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1016204#post1016204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering. What about big tech-machinery stuff ? Imean the huge teleportation device. Could the Observer be satisfied by technology enabling teleportation ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. The Consensus doesn't accept just ANYTHING as Coincidental if it has a technological Focus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T13:33:48-08:00","id":1016219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1016199#post1016199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HDYDT so commonly gives bad advice. I'm not saying the Batman wouldn't work, but you really have to take everything that book says with a grain of salt. The whole thing about not being seen is questionable.<br /> <br /> The thing is, even in HAP you usually can't hide from the hypothetical observer. There are ways but they usually feel like they are pushing the edges of the allowable. If there is a vantage point one can reasonably sit and say WTF from, it is Vulgar W/O Witnesses. So he question isn't how do you hide yourself from the Hypothetical Observer, it is how do you make every potential Hypothetical Observer think something normal happened?<br /> <br /> People get disoriented with sudden light changes, so you change the lights. People lose track of each other in a crowd, so you run into a crowd. If an observer could reasonably believe that he just lost sight of you in that instant, congrats, you've reached coincidental for the departure. If an observer could reasonably believe he just hadn't noticed you before, congrats, you've reached coincidental for the arrival.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One problem with the &quot;people lose track of each other in a crowd&quot; part. You're surrounded by potential witnesses in a crowd, all of whom may be looking right at you as you just magically stop being right in front of them. Whether they see you or not is a difference between V+W and plain Vulgar, but it wouldn't make sense for that to become coincidental.<br /> <br /> That's the thing about the HAP, the passerby may be anywhere, even right next to you. The only places they may not be are places where Schrodinger's Cat could reasonably be argued. e.g.. I have an empty box, I really need to pull a gun from it, no one knows what's in the box as it hasn't been opened. I have a gun in my gunsafe at home, I can put my hand in the box and either teleport my hand to inside the safe, or teleport the gun to my hand. Coincidental as while the box is closed and unobserved, the gun may or may not be in there until revealed. Similarly for the safe a gun may or may not be in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T13:51:22-08:00","id":1016226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1016219#post1016219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One problem with the &quot;people lose track of each other in a crowd&quot; part. You're surrounded by potential witnesses in a crowd, all of whom may be looking right at you as you just magically stop being right in front of them. Whether they see you or not is a difference between V+W and plain Vulgar, but it wouldn't make sense for that to become coincidental.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's arguable. This is the World of Darkness. Nobody cares, and nobody sees unless they want to. Hidden in plain sight would not work in our world. Not sure it would not in the WoD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1016212#post1016212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think so. The Consensus doesn't accept just ANYTHING as Coincidental if it has a technological Focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know... :'( This is kinda sad though ^^ Well may be it would be vulgar to teleport whole human beings or living things, but there is research on teleportation. May be tiny objects could be coincidentally teleported with Tech. Dunno...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T16:10:07-08:00","id":1016301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1016226#post1016226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's arguable. This is the World of Darkness. Nobody cares, and nobody sees unless they want to. Hidden in plain sight would not work in our world. Not sure it would not in the WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure that's how HAP works. It's more &quot;what would someone think if they saw it&quot; rather than &quot;What someone would think if they gave a damn&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T19:07:21-08:00","id":1016355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1016219#post1016219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> One problem with the &quot;people lose track of each other in a crowd&quot; part. You're surrounded by potential witnesses in a crowd, all of whom may be looking right at you as you just magically stop being right in front of them. Whether they see you or not is a difference between V+W and plain Vulgar, but it wouldn't make sense for that to become coincidental.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the average perceiver is standing right next to the disappearing person though, I think the HAP is on that street or square or room or wherever. If the HAP is that close to anything that could possibly happen, they may as well be a HOP. If someone actually <i>is </i>looking in that situation though, it would go straight from Coincidental to Vulgar with Witnesses. Good Alertness, Awareness, Stealth, and/or Arcane would be useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T19:48:26-08:00","id":1016366,"title":"","content":"You might be able to justify disappearing in a crown as coincidental if you add Entropy 2 to the Effect. By manipulating luck, you make it so you disappear the moment everyone immediately around you (ie the only ones who could actually see you) are looking away. The fact that it's in a bustling crowd, where people fade in and out of view constantly and without rhyme or reason could help sell the Effect. Anyone could appear or disappear at any time when you aren't looking directly at them. It's just how crowds work.<br /> <br /> Then again, I prefer a more flexible interpretation of coincidental and vulgar, simply because making every little thing vulgar seems less fun.<br /> <br /> As for pulling a Batman and disappearing in the darkness or obscuring smoke, I'm inclined to lean on the Mythic Threads here. Throwing a smoke bomb or flashbang and disappearing isn't just possible, it's an established trope. There's weight there, which can make all the difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T08:54:26-08:00","id":1016580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1016219#post1016219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> One problem with the &quot;people lose track of each other in a crowd&quot; part. You're surrounded by potential witnesses in a crowd, all of whom may be looking right at you as you just magically stop being right in front of them. Whether they see you or not is a difference between V+W and plain Vulgar, but it wouldn't make sense for that to become coincidental.<br /> <br /> That's the thing about the HAP, the passerby may be anywhere, even right next to you. The only places they may not be are places where Schrodinger's Cat could reasonably be argued. e.g.. I have an empty box, I really need to pull a gun from it, no one knows what's in the box as it hasn't been opened. I have a gun in my gunsafe at home, I can put my hand in the box and either teleport my hand to inside the safe, or teleport the gun to my hand. Coincidental as while the box is closed and unobserved, the gun may or may not be in there until revealed. Similarly for the safe a gun may or may not be in there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you ever seen the studies on how easy it is to lose track of a moving object in a chaotic situation. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vJG698U2Mvo\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vJG698U2Mvo\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vJG698U2Mvo\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vJG698U2Mvo </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Maybe you didn't miss anything in that video. Lots of people do.<br /> <br /> We like to think our senses are very definite; that like a camera if something is in frame it shows up and if it is not it does not. That's simply not the case. The brain lies and everyone knows it. The average person is very used to losing track of objects and even other people in a crowd. Since the hypothetical observer is an average person, she is used to that too. Give either of them to doubt their senses or to focus on something else and they will. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T09:29:18-08:00","id":1016601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1016580#post1016580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you ever seen the studies on how easy it is to lose track of a moving object in a chaotic situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vJG698U2Mvo\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vJG698U2Mvo\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vJG698U2Mvo\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vJG698U2Mvo </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Maybe you didn't miss anything in that video. Lots of people do.<br /> <br /> We like to think our senses are very definite; that like a camera if something is in frame it shows up and if it is not it does not. That's simply not the case. The brain lies and everyone knows it. The average person is very used to losing track of objects and even other people in a crowd. Since the hypothetical observer is an average person, she is used to that too. Give either of them to doubt their senses or to focus on something else and they will.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>See, to me that would be a good justification for while Teleporting out of a crowd can be Vulgar without Witnesses. But when determining Vulgar vs Coincidental, HAP asks the question &quot;If someone saw this, what would they think&quot;.<br /> <br /> The assumption for HAP is someone DID notice. Otherwise you could make the argument that changing your skin colour or hair colour from pale/blond to dark in the blink of an eye is coincidental because not a lot of people may be paying attention to that, or that you can shrink a statue to pocket-sized coincidentally because people are bad a judging perspective.<br /> <br /> HAP assumes someone saw exactly what you did regardless of where you were at the time of doing it. How this person judges it may depend on the active consensus, and that may shift Vulgar to Coincidental or vice versa, but the point is it's assumed to be seen.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T10:47:38-08:00","id":1016640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1016601#post1016601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, to me that would be a good justification for while Teleporting out of a crowd can be Vulgar without Witnesses. But when determining Vulgar vs Coincidental, HAP asks the question &quot;If someone saw this, what would they think&quot;.<br /> <br /> The assumption for HAP is someone DID notice. Otherwise you could make the argument that changing your skin colour or hair colour from pale/blond to dark in the blink of an eye is coincidental because not a lot of people may be paying attention to that, or that you can shrink a statue to pocket-sized coincidentally because people are bad a judging perspective.<br /> <br /> HAP assumes someone saw exactly what you did regardless of where you were at the time of doing it. How this person judges it may depend on the active consensus, and that may shift Vulgar to Coincidental or vice versa, but the point is it's assumed to be seen.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, the assumption for HAP (and even HOP for that matter) is that someone saw, not someone noticed. If you are already doing something on the street in front of a bunch of arbitrary witnesses and they don't notice anything wrong, that's strong evidence that your spell is Coincidental. There are exceptions of course, but they tend to be based on pretty obvious issues (your real witnesses were atypical, there was another angle of view that made everything clear, etc.).<br /> <br /> It's all about expectations. Expectations are why listening to a far away voice with a cell phone is coincidental but listening to a far away voice with a seashell is vulgar. It's the same effect, but one plays into what people expect to see. People are used to losing track of each other in crowds, so they don't blink when it happens.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T11:35:03-08:00","id":1016663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1016640#post1016640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree, the assumption for HAP (and even HOP for that matter) is that someone saw, not someone noticed. If you are already doing something on the street in front of a bunch of arbitrary witnesses and they don't notice anything wrong, that's strong evidence that your spell is Coincidental. There are exceptions of course, but they tend to be based on pretty obvious issues (your real witnesses were atypical, there was another angle of view that made everything clear, etc.).<br /> <br /> It's all about expectations. Expectations are why listening to a far away voice with a cell phone is coincidental but listening to a far away voice with a seashell is vulgar. It's the same effect, but one plays into what people expect to see. People are used to losing track of each other in crowds, so they don't blink when it happens.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>By that logic, you could have a mage do any magic as coincidental so long as they don't notice. Put up a mind effect so no one pays attention to you, and viola, you're free to turn carrots into babies without a point of paradox since no one will notice.<br /> <br /> <br /> And yes, people are used to losing track of people in a crowd. But it's not just the perspective of someone watching the crowd you need to pay attention to, it's the people that make up that crowd too. If you're walking along, and a guy just runs in front of you and then vanishes, you're not going to think &quot;Oh my, I must have lost him in the crowd&quot; you're going to think &quot;Wait, what just happened? Was that real?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T12:17:04-08:00","id":1016676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1016663#post1016663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By that logic, you could have a mage do any magic as coincidental so long as they don't notice. Put up a mind effect so no one pays attention to you, and viola, you're free to turn carrots into babies without a point of paradox since no one will notice.<br /> <br /> <br /> And yes, people are used to losing track of people in a crowd. But it's not just the perspective of someone watching the crowd you need to pay attention to, it's the people that make up that crowd too. If you're walking along, and a guy just runs in front of you and then vanishes, you're not going to think &quot;Oh my, I must have lost him in the crowd&quot; you're going to think &quot;Wait, what just happened? Was that real?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's not the matter here I think. Vashing in a crowd is a &quot;saying&quot;. There is belief around it, and especially in the WoD, I can see how it can be coincidental. That does not mean that all Effects performed in a crowd works coincidentally. Of course, if the guy just runs in front of you, this is not applicable. We're talking about the case you want to melt in the crowd, and vanishes doing it. It can works because the idea of someone desappearing in a crowd full of poeple actually exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T12:24:28-08:00","id":1016680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1016663#post1016663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By that logic, you could have a mage do any magic as coincidental so long as they don't notice. Put up a mind effect so no one pays attention to you, and viola, you're free to turn carrots into babies without a point of paradox since no one will notice.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can figure out how to target the hypothetical observer, sure. But since he's a gaming abstraction in another world, I don't see that happening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yes, people are used to losing track of people in a crowd. But it's not just the perspective of someone watching the crowd you need to pay attention to, it's the people that make up that crowd too. If you're walking along, and a guy just runs in front of you and then vanishes, you're not going to think &quot;Oh my, I must have lost him in the crowd&quot; you're going to think &quot;Wait, what just happened? Was that real?&quot; </div> </div> </div>People in the crowd lose each other in the crowd all the time too. Anyone who has been driving only to realize the person they thought they passed is in front of them again is familiar with that. Anyone who has lost track of a friend in a mall or park is familiar with that. Your example would be rather attention grabbing (and not the only thing teleportation could look like), and there would always be the risk that you'd pick up the attention of someone more suspicious than most, but if you are doing the things people already do to get lost in a crowd you should be in a good position to slide out of the average crowd's perception without being noticed.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T12:27:48-08:00","id":1016681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1016676#post1016676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that's not the matter here I think. Vashing in a crowd is a &quot;saying&quot;. There is belief around it, and especially in the WoD, I can see how it can be coincidental. That does not mean that all Effects performed in a crowd works coincidentally. Of course, if the guy just runs in front of you, this is not applicable. We're talking about the case you want to melt in the crowd, and vanishes doing it. It can works because the idea of someone desappearing in a crowd full of poeple actually exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>We also have the saying &quot;raining cats and dogs&quot; but that doesn't mean turning falling rain water into canines would be coincidental.<br /> <br /> You can make the argument of using Mind to make people unable to track you after entering a crowd, basically giving you a level or two of temporary Arcane, as coincidental. But actually teleporting with Corr 3 because you're &quot;vanishing into the crowd&quot; is a bit much.<br /> <br /> Also, if this were allowed, it could be so easily exploited. Why stop at Corr 3? If this is allowed, why not transform into air when &quot;vanishing into the crowd&quot;, why not become invisible when &quot;vanishing into the crowd&quot;, why not stop time and walk away while &quot;vanishing into the crowd&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T12:50:23-08:00","id":1016688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1016681#post1016681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We also have the saying &quot;raining cats and dogs&quot; but that doesn't mean turning falling rain water into canines would be coincidental.<br /> <br /> You can make the argument of using Mind to make people unable to track you after entering a crowd, basically giving you a level or two of temporary Arcane, as coincidental. But actually teleporting with Corr 3 because you're &quot;vanishing into the crowd&quot; is a bit much.<br /> <br /> Also, if this were allowed, it could be so easily exploited. Why stop at Corr 3? If this is allowed, why not transform into air when &quot;vanishing into the crowd&quot;, why not become invisible when &quot;vanishing into the crowd&quot;, why not stop time and walk away while &quot;vanishing into the crowd&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I get your point, but I'm sure you make the difference between &quot;vanishing into a crowd&quot;, and &quot;raining cats and dogs&quot;...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T14:20:15-08:00","id":1016733,"title":"","content":"The issue is that &quot;vanishing into a crowd,&quot; by making yourself less likely to be seen is different from literally making it rain animals. &quot;Vanishing into a crowd,&quot; by literally vanishing isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T14:28:29-08:00","id":1016736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1016226#post1016226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I know... :'( This is kinda sad though ^^ Well may be it would be vulgar to teleport whole human beings or living things, but there is research on teleportation. May be tiny objects could be coincidentally teleported with Tech. Dunno...</div> </div> </div> </div>Consensus is about humanity's shared expectations, not about possible through science. If you construct an apparatus able to actually teleport tiny things without magic, it will work without Paradox for being real, sure. But will also make most people believe you simply played a trick, because they don't expect that to be possible. So an effect that mimics the very same device, but in the end is awakened magic, will be Vulgar still. You mimic a possibility, but not an expected one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T16:41:55-08:00","id":1016806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1016681#post1016681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if this were allowed, it could be so easily exploited. Why stop at Corr 3? If this is allowed, why not transform into air when &amp;quot;vanishing into the crowd&amp;quot;, why not become invisible when &amp;quot;vanishing into the crowd&amp;quot;, why not stop time and walk away while &amp;quot;vanishing into the crowd&amp;quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, as long as the reconstitution of your normal state is also plausible to the HAP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T19:18:33-08:00","id":1016868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1016806#post1016806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, as long as the reconstitution of your normal state is also plausible to the HAP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just find another crowd to materialise in. If you can vanish in a crowd, who says you can't reappear in a crowd...<br /> <br /> And if that works for you, then congratulations, you've adopted a system where magic is coincidental at rush hour.<br /> What in the world would the Technocracy think about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T19:48:48-08:00","id":1016875,"title":"","content":"There are still some things that would be too flagrant, and I'd still say if someone in the crowd is <i>actually</i> looking, then it's V+W. Probably not worth the risk most of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T20:53:04-08:00","id":1016896,"title":"","content":"... That's sort of the whole point of the H in HAP. If someone was watching and it would be vulgar with witnesses, then nobody watching makes it vulgar without witnesses, not coincidental...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T05:18:31-08:00","id":1016993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1016875#post1016875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are still some things that would be too flagrant, and I'd still say if someone in the crowd is <i>actually</i> looking, then it's V+W. Probably not worth the risk most of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1016896#post1016896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... That's sort of the whole point of the H in HAP. If someone was watching and it would be vulgar with witnesses, then nobody watching makes it vulgar without witnesses, not coincidental...</div> </div> </div> </div>There's always been the possibility of an atypical sleeper turning a coincidental spell vulgar. If you remove the bullets from someone's gun the average person wouldn't notice the weight difference when they drew it, soldiers and other people who spent a lot of time practicing would. If you are performing card tricks using awakened magic most sleepers won't notice, professional magicians would. In certain rare circumstances, those effects would be vulgar, but since we aren't going to choose a professional soldier-magician as our hypothetical observer, at least one of those two effects will default to coincidental.<br /> <br /> I do agree that disappearing into a crowd should carry some risk of being noticed, much like mundane means of doing the same don't always work. So perhaps a stealth role to get 'into' the crowd might be necessary, but once the mage is 'in' disappearing falls well on the side of coincidence as far as most Sleepers are concerned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T06:11:39-08:00","id":1017016,"title":"","content":"There are numerous exemples in films. Someone is pursuing a guy who disappears in a crowd. He asks randomly if someone has seen him. Usually, nobody did. Nobody says it's magical, not even you who are behind the screen, watching the movie as the absolute witness of the scene. Though, the guy did desappear...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T07:25:23-08:00","id":1017051,"title":"","content":"Ok, so conceptually you're not going to be swayed on the whole &quot;Corr 3 teleportation is inherently vulgar&quot; side of things.<br /> Let's look at it from a gameplay perspective then. One of the reasons you'd want Corr 3 teleportation to always be vulgar is to discourage your players from abusing it. If all it took was a crowd of people for it to be coincidental, then it would be really easy for the mage to go anywhere in the world, so long as there's a crowd. Every city would now be within reach. You'd be able to travel from New York to Tokyo in the blink of a traffic light without having to worry about accumulating paradox.<br /> <br /> What would this do to a game? Well, it would serve as a quick &quot;get out of trouble&quot; scheme, removing all tension in any city based chase. Oh no, a group of Technocratic Agents are after me, that's ok, I'll just run into the crowd and end up in Nairobi, no problem here!<br /> If it was vulgar, then it would be more a question of &quot;Do I take the quick and dirty way out and risk the backlash, or do I find a more reality friendly approach?&quot;<br /> <br /> It would also cheapen travel significantly. We need to assist in a pan-european smuggling operation. That's not a problem, I can go from London, to Rome, then to Athens, Luxembourg, Warsaw, Vilnius, and Valletta, and get back in time for tea tomorrow without a single concern for paradox. While I'm at it, I could stop by Beijing for dumplings. Any particular tea you want while I'm there?<br /> Why would you ever take mundane transport if Corr 3 between major cities was coincidental? Heck, even teleportation within cities has become inconsequential . Need to get to the other side of town? Find a crowd in the nearby mall, appear in the convention hall, and viola, nothing matters to you.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then, if we start to include other methods of &quot;vanishing into the crowd&quot; such as turning into air, or heck turning into a bird, then crowds become a weird kind of Node like place to do magic. &quot;Uh oh, he's getting away! Quick, let's find a crowd to transform in!&quot;<br /> It sort of flies in the face of the entire point of subtle magic, which is sleepers as an obstacle to be navigated around. Yes Reality Zones and gathering acolytes can turn otherwise vulgar effects into coincidental ones. But that's the sort of thing that needs to be earned, either through a lot of research into the local superstitions, or though careful grooming. Just having any crowd serve as &quot;This is the place &quot;vanishing&quot; magic is coincidental&quot; ad hoc subverts this quite drastically.<br /> <br /> <br /> Listing all this stuff does create an interesting number of gameplay scenarios. Perhaps a mage can use crowds and other psychological blindspots as focus of sorts for magic, under the idea that reality is only static for as long as someone is actively observing it. But it should still be vulgar, if not for the simple reason that paradox is a necessary component of this game, required to prevent magic trivialising everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 12-14-2016, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T08:31:18-08:00","id":1017085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1017051#post1017051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so conceptually you're not going to be swayed on the whole &quot;Corr 3 teleportation is inherently vulgar&quot; side of things.<br /> Let's look at it from a gameplay perspective then. One of the reasons you'd want Corr 3 teleportation to always be vulgar is to discourage your players from abusing it. If all it took was a crowd of people for it to be coincidental, then it would be really easy for the mage to go anywhere in the world, so long as there's a crowd. Every city would now be within reach. You'd be able to travel from New York to Tokyo in the blink of a traffic light without having to worry about accumulating paradox.<br /> <br /> What would this do to a game? Well, it would serve as a quick &quot;get out of trouble&quot; scheme, removing all tension in any city based chase. Oh no, a group of Technocratic Agents are after me, that's ok, I'll just run into the crowd and end up in Nairobi, no problem here!<br /> If it was vulgar, then it would be more a question of &quot;Do I take the quick and dirty way out and risk the backlash, or do I find a more reality friendly approach?&quot;<br /> <br /> It would also cheapen travel significantly. We need to assist in a pan-european smuggling operation. That's not a problem, I can go from London, to Rome, then to Athens, Luxembourg, Warsaw, Vilnius, and Valletta, and get back in time for tea tomorrow without a single concern for paradox. While I'm at it, I could stop by Beijing for dumplings. Any particular tea you wan while I'm there?<br /> Why would you ever take mundane transport if Corr 3 between major cities was coincidental? Heck, even teleportation within cities has become conscienceless. Need to get to the other side of town? Find a crowd in the nearby mall, appear in the convention hall, and viola, nothing matters to you.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Listing all this stuff does create an interesting number of gameplay scenarios. Perhaps a mage can use crowds and other psychological blindspots as focus of sorts for magic, under the idea that reality is only static for as long as someone is actively observing it. But it should still be vulgar, if not for the simple reason that paradox is a necessary component of this game, required to prevent magic trivialising everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are conflating coincidental with trivial. Sure coincidental is easier than vulgar, but you still need to take into teleportation range difficulty, choosing your destination point, making sure other Mages don't track you, surveillance cameras, flashy magic styles, etc. There are a whole host of reasons why even if you could be 100% certain your teleports were coincidental every single time, you'd still want to use a sanctum or node instead of a crowd. <br /> <br /> And as for game balance, I'm not a big fan of kludging paradox rules just because something seems too easy. There are enough in game impediments that provide much more story potential.. Besides, when you take into account things like sanctums and nodes and allies, smuggling should be a minor endeavor for any well connected Mage. Some things that would be major hurdles in any other game line just aren't a problem in this one.<br /> <br /> Not sure I'd let crowds be used as a coincidental way of turning into birds, though. That's not something commonly associated with crowds. Perhaps if the spell made you teleport and change form at the same time, and there was a flock of birds nearby. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T09:18:17-08:00","id":1017106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1017085#post1017085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are conflating coincidental with trivial. Sure coincidental is easier than vulgar, but you still need to take into teleportation range difficulty, choosing your destination point, making sure other Mages don't track you, surveillance cameras, flashy magic styles, etc. There are a whole host of reasons why even if you could be 100% certain your teleports were coincidental every single time, you'd still want to use a sanctum or node instead of a crowd.<br /> <br /> And as for game balance, I'm not a big fan of kludging paradox rules just because something seems too easy. There are enough in game impediments that provide much more story potential.. Besides, when you take into account things like sanctums and nodes and allies, smuggling should be a minor endeavor for any well connected Mage. Some things that would be major hurdles in any other game line just aren't a problem in this one.<br /> <br /> Not sure I'd let crowds be used as a coincidental way of turning into birds, though. That's not something commonly associated with crowds. Perhaps if the spell made you teleport and change form at the same time, and there was a flock of birds nearby.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was focusing more on consequence than difficulty. On that point, doing magic by a node doesn't change the amount of paradox one would receive for a vulgar effect, nor whether an effect is coincidental or not.<br /> <br /> Also, Sanctums are not something that a lot of people have access to. They are highly specialised pockets of reality, even more specialised than Reality Zones, that take years to foster and require constant upkeep to maintain. They only tend to work for one mage (an the few who have similar enough an outlook as she does), and tend not to be well advertised due to their potency.<br /> Yes it takes time to do Corr 3 stuff, but making it coincidental just makes that much less of a problem.<br /> <br /> You're not a fan of paradox being the main obstacle and consideration for mages doing magic? What game have you been playing?<br /> <br /> Oh boy, so you're ok with Corr 3 being the gateway sphere to coincidental transformation? Neat way to avoid Permanent Paradox there. Perhaps you could use this to teleport into comicon and give yourself all kinds of sweet bodymods like wings, Agg soaking skin and clothes and whatnot and have that be coincidental too, continuing to avoid permanent paradox. Then you'd have a somewhat convoluted yet pretty doable method of passing the gauntlet without having to worry about the avatar storm at all. (doesn't matter what you think about the avatar storm, the point is that, if you did like having the avatar storm in your game, allowing coincidental Corr 3 infused transformation in this manner would be a way to completely trivialise it).<br /> <br /> Hey, for that matter, Stepping sideways in a crowd could be considered coincidental by the same token. All you need is a crowd of people walking around a gauntlet lowered place, and hey presto, you can sidestep without doxing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T09:41:54-08:00","id":1017111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1016993#post1016993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's always been the possibility of an atypical sleeper turning a coincidental spell vulgar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Has there? Since when?<br /> <br /> Esp. since there isn't retroactive vulgarity. If an atypical Sleeper notices something after the fact, there's other ways it gets handled.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you remove the bullets from someone's gun the average person wouldn't notice the weight difference when they drew it, soldiers and other people who spent a lot of time practicing would. </div> </div> </div>How does that change the vulgarity? They didn't notice you remove the bullets, only that the bullets aren't there. If an expert marksman pulls a gun they think is loaded only to feel that it isn't, they're just going to assume they made a mistake and it wasn't loaded.<br /> <br /> If you remove the bullets after the gun is drawn, they'd notice, but so would an untrained individual because that's just a basic sensory input; the gun suddenly got lighter for not reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you are performing card tricks using awakened magic most sleepers won't notice, professional magicians would. </div> </div> </div>Why? If their naturally coincidental, how would the professional magician see anything other than someone that's really good and might even have some new tricks to try to study. Magicians are constantly trying to come up with (and hide how from their peers) new tricks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So perhaps a stealth role to get 'into' the crowd might be necessary, but once the mage is 'in' disappearing falls well on the side of coincidence as far as most Sleepers are concerned. </div> </div> </div>How is literally vanishing into thin air ever coincidental to a Sleeper? Sleepers don't believe that you can walk into a crowd and &quot;poof&quot; vanish. They believe you can walk into a crowd and be impossible to track. Not the same thing. Nobody actually believes, &quot;vanishes into a crowd,&quot; is a literal statement of physically ceasing to be capable of being noticed.<br /> <br /> Walking into a crowd is a great way to do a huge number of stealth-focused effects to get away from people trying to follow you, but not teleportation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1017016#post1017016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are numerous exemples in films. Someone is pursuing a guy who disappears in a crowd. He asks randomly if someone has seen him. Usually, nobody did. Nobody says it's magical, not even you who are behind the screen, watching the movie as the absolute witness of the scene. Though, the guy did desappear...</div> </div> </div> </div>The movie is shot so you can't see the guy, the movie doesn't posit he literally vanished/teleported unless it's a supernatural/superpowers movie (at which point it really doesn't apply because those don't tend to worry about this stuff/follow Mage's rules about it).<br /> <br /> Again, nobody actually thinks, &quot;I didn't see the guy, so clearly he's invisible/capable of teleportation/etc.&quot; they think, &quot;I didn't see the guy, so he must have blended in so well I didn't notice him.&quot; Nobody says it's magical, because it's not magical to duck into a crowd and be hard to spot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T09:59:56-08:00","id":1017123,"title":"","content":"Let's do this point by point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1017051#post1017051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so conceptually you're not going to be swayed on the whole &quot;Corr 3 teleportation is inherently vulgar&quot; side of things.<br /> Let's look at it from a gameplay perspective then.</div> </div> </div> </div>I selmdom do. But I will follow anyway to explain myself more precisely. There are misunderstandings there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1017051#post1017051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the reasons you'd want Corr 3 teleportation to always be vulgar is to discourage your players from abusing it. If all it took was a crowd of people for it to be coincidental, then it would be really easy for the mage to go anywhere in the world, so long as there's a crowd. Every city would now be within reach. You'd be able to travel from New York to Tokyo in the blink of a traffic light without having to worry about accumulating paradox.<br /> <br /> What would this do to a game? Well, it would serve as a quick &quot;get out of trouble&quot; scheme, removing all tension in any city based chase. Oh no, a group of Technocratic Agents are after me, that's ok, I'll just run into the crowd and end up in Nairobi, no problem here!<br /> If it was vulgar, then it would be more a question of &quot;Do I take the quick and dirty way out and risk the backlash, or do I find a more reality friendly approach?&quot;<br /> <br /> It would also cheapen travel significantly. We need to assist in a pan-european smuggling operation. That's not a problem, I can go from London, to Rome, then to Athens, Luxembourg, Warsaw, Vilnius, and Valletta, and get back in time for tea tomorrow without a single concern for paradox. While I'm at it, I could stop by Beijing for dumplings. Any particular tea you want while I'm there?<br /> Why would you ever take mundane transport if Corr 3 between major cities was coincidental? Heck, even teleportation within cities has become inconsequential . Need to get to the other side of town? Find a crowd in the nearby mall, appear in the convention hall, and viola, nothing matters to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no trouble with players abusing it. They're Mages and have powers beyond what most could possibly imagine. This is not a problem for me. However, I can assure you that I will not accept it right away. Actually, using the &quot;vanishing in a crowd trick&quot; implies that the Mage believes he can desappear this way. This is very limiting. I have a Verbena witch in one of my games. She will definitely not do that, ever. This is completely outside her paradigm. To simplify, let's say that it is something that John Courage could do, but that's because he actually believes in that sort of things.<br /> <br /> One other thing, I never considered teleporting being a problem in any of my sessions mainly for three reasons:<br /> - For one, I insist on the sympathetic link factor. Using Correspondance, yes, but not without knowing your target. If you never went to Roma, you cannot teleport there without the proper ritual to accumulate enough successes because you do not know the place. Using this trick of the crowd is mostly a thing of the instant. So... using it to get home is one thing, but going to other places is another. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> said, coincidental and easy are two different things,<br /> - Then, when you play a game where characters can teleport, having objectives like going somewhere or killing someone, or something like this is not possible. As a ST, I force myself to come up with new intrigues that need the players to do much more than teleporting to get what they want. If I write a scenario where my players can use that solution, I consider that I failed them,<br /> - Finally, even with that trick, there are plenty of things to discourage the players to use it. You could use counter magick: the thecnocrats following the Mages can use a device controlling some sort of camera network to instantly follow the Mage due to its moving signature and making them enable to follow him anywhere. Or a device to disturb spacetime to prevent the Mage to teleport (like a Ward), or traps of the like.<br /> <br /> The thing of the ward is something I already used and it functions well. My players were trying to follow a NWO who abducted an important NPC. The Virtual Adept of the game tried to locate him with a Correspondance Effect (he had a sympathetic link with said NPC), but I wanted that part to go longer, so I told him that he encountered unexpected difficulties with a firewall (it actually was a protective Ward). I played it like I would have played a car chase with opposing rolls.<br /> <br /> Actually, this is also true with Time Effects. If my players can solve a mystery using Time visions, it's because the mystery was not complex enough. I tend to describe Time Effects in a way it can often be misinterpreted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1017051#post1017051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then, if we start to include other methods of &quot;vanishing into the crowd&quot; such as turning into air, or heck turning into a bird, then crowds become a weird kind of Node like place to do magic. &quot;Uh oh, he's getting away! Quick, let's find a crowd to transform in!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, the Mage needs to believe that there is some sort of connection. You already heard the expression &quot;vanishing in a crowd&quot;, but I bet you never heard &quot;turning into a bird in a crowd&quot;. In the end, that Effect is coincidental when you can justify it by your pratice. Most of the time, the Mages would not even know how to do it. And to answer someone else, I would at least require a successful Stealth roll first. Having Arcane background can also make the thing easier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1017051#post1017051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Listing all this stuff does create an interesting number of gameplay scenarios. Perhaps a mage can use crowds and other psychological blindspots as focus of sorts for magic, under the idea that reality is only static for as long as someone is actively observing it. But it should still be vulgar, if not for the simple reason that paradox is a necessary component of this game, required to prevent magic trivialising everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personnally do not understand Paradox that way. I always thought that Paradox was the safegard for Mages. A way to prevent things to go mad in a game. And if you do not want your Mages to make Magick trivial, you can always use narrative reasons to prevent them doing so:<br /> - There is the easy solution of Technocracts wanting to chase them,<br /> - But you can also use other things like making the wintesses part of the game: Someone saw the Effect and that one now wants to cry it to everyone ready to listen to him. You can make that kind of situations nightmares for your players, making them think twice about risking it that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T10:01:37-08:00","id":1017124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1017111#post1017111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The movie is shot so you can't see the guy, the movie doesn't posit he literally vanished/teleported unless it's a supernatural/superpowers movie (at which point it really doesn't apply because those don't tend to worry about this stuff/follow Mage's rules about it).<br /> <br /> Again, nobody actually thinks, &quot;I didn't see the guy, so clearly he's invisible/capable of teleportation/etc.&quot; they think, &quot;I didn't see the guy, so he must have blended in so well I didn't notice him.&quot; Nobody says it's magical, because it's not magical to duck into a crowd and be hard to spot.</div> </div> </div> </div>May be that was not the best exemple ever, but I think you got my point ^^ <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T10:20:24-08:00","id":1017135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1017106#post1017106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was focusing more on consequence than difficulty. On that point, doing magic by a node doesn't change the amount of paradox one would receive for a vulgar effect, nor whether an effect is coincidental or not.<br /> <br /> Also, Sanctums are not something that a lot of people have access to. They are highly specialised pockets of reality, even more specialised than Reality Zones, that take years to foster and require constant upkeep to maintain. They only tend to work for one mage (an the few who have similar enough an outlook as she does), and tend not to be well advertised due to their potency.<br /> Yes it takes time to do Corr 3 stuff, but making it coincidental just makes that much less of a problem.<br /> <br /> You're not a fan of paradox being the main obstacle and consideration for mages doing magic? What game have you been playing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a fan of altering the rationale for Paradox just because something rustles my jimmies. As for what game I've been playing: The one where the Technocracy actually has major issues with reality deviants and is capable of hunting them down. The one where reality is flexible enough to get really strange if you push it the right way. The one where crazy stuff is possible if you are willing to risk burning like icarus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh boy, so you're ok with Corr 3 being the gateway sphere to coincidental transformation? Neat way to avoid Permanent Paradox there. Perhaps you could use this to teleport into comicon and give yourself all kinds of sweet bodymods like wings, Agg soaking skin and clothes and whatnot and have that be coincidental too, continuing to avoid permanent paradox. Then you'd have a somewhat convoluted yet pretty doable method of passing the gauntlet without having to worry about the avatar storm at all. (doesn't matter what you think about the avatar storm, the point is that, if you did like having the avatar storm in your game, allowing coincidental Corr 3 infused transformation in this manner would be a way to completely trivialise it). </div> </div> </div>You keep trying to do this thing where you post what you think is an outrageous and unavoidable consequence, which is either not outrageous or not unavoidable. Firstly, I don't think the Perma-dox rules have anything to do with vulgarity, otherwise just casting the spell in your sanctum would bypass all of that. Secondly, people with real wings do not walk around Comicon, and the good costumes tend to attract attention anyways, so they are the opposite of what you want to do to use a crowd coincidentally. I wouldn't allow it. And even if I did, if it did break the game just having a Sanctum would break it too. <br /> <br /> If a mage wants to rack up massive Perma-dox while engaging in behaviors that could blow up in his face in an instant, I view that as a self correcting problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hey, for that matter, Stepping sideways in a crowd could be considered coincidental by the same token. All you need is a crowd of people walking around a gauntlet lowered place, and hey presto, you can sidestep without doxing. </div> </div> </div>I'd be fine with it if the mage in question could do it in a way that looked right. However, crossing the gauntlet is already specifically called out as vulgar, and its appearance is already determined. So, no, unfortunately no.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T11:14:52-08:00","id":1017161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1017111#post1017111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Has there? Since when?<br /> <br /> Esp. since there isn't retroactive vulgarity. If an atypical Sleeper notices something after the fact, there's other ways it gets handled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, chose a bad example with the soldier although I should point out that someone unfamiliar with guns is unlikely to know what the change in weight is between shots. If you empty their gun at that point, the example still holds. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why? If their naturally coincidental, how would the professional magician see anything other than someone that's really good and might even have some new tricks to try to study. Magicians are constantly trying to come up with (and hide how from their peers) new tricks. </div> </div> </div>And if you are using the mask of stage magic to do something that would be vulgar without it? You are going to have a harder time fooling an expert than you are fooling the typical person. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How is literally vanishing into thin air ever coincidental to a Sleeper? Sleepers don't believe that you can walk into a crowd and &quot;poof&quot; vanish. They believe you can walk into a crowd and be impossible to track. Not the same thing. Nobody actually believes, &quot;vanishes into a crowd,&quot; is a literal statement of physically ceasing to be capable of being noticed. </div> </div> </div>When a sleeper sees something that doesn't add up, there are two paths they can go: they can assume that their senses are wrong or they can assume that reality is. The latter causes something to be vulgar, the former does not. The books show repeated examples of mages exploiting the former to cast spells coincidentally. The cabal that carries a 'Filming in Progress' sign around L.A. is a notable example. People see the impossible, but there's a reason to disbelieve their eyes at hand so they aren't worried.<br /> <br /> Our senses do not provide a perfect picture of the world. We get false positives and false negatives all the time and our brains are constantly updating our mental image. It isn't unusual at all to not see something one second and see it the next, or vice versa. That's how you can miss seeing the milk when it is right in front of you, or see a glimpse of a face in the tree branches. If the situation is confusing enough that can be reason for large numbers of people to miss even big things. Crowds are one area this happens. It's not that people don't see the mage disappear, it's that they are seeing everyone disappear and reappear all the time. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Walking into a crowd is a great way to do a huge number of stealth-focused effects to get away from people trying to follow you, but not teleportation. </div> </div> </div>If teleportation is visually indistinguishable from stealth, why wouldn't it get the same benefit?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, nobody actually thinks, &quot;I didn't see the guy, so clearly he's invisible/capable of teleportation/etc.&quot; they think, &quot;I didn't see the guy, so he must have blended in so well I didn't notice him.&quot; Nobody says it's magical, because it's not magical to duck into a crowd and be hard to spot. </div> </div> </div>The fact that people would grab for the latter over the former is precisely why blending into a crowd works as a coincidental<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T11:33:21-08:00","id":1017180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1017161#post1017161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a sleeper sees something that doesn't add up, there are two paths they can go: they can assume that their senses are wrong or they can assume that reality is. The latter causes something to be vulgar, the former does not. The books show repeated examples of mages exploiting the former to cast spells coincidentally. The cabal that carries a 'Filming in Progress' sign around L.A. is a notable example. People see the impossible, but there's a reason to disbelieve their eyes at hand so they aren't worried.<br /> <br /> Our senses do not provide a perfect picture of the world. We get false positives and false negatives all the time and our brains are constantly updating our mental image. It isn't unusual at all to not see something one second and see it the next, or vice versa. That's how you can miss seeing the milk when it is right in front of you, or see a glimpse of a face in the tree branches. If the situation is confusing enough that can be reason for large numbers of people to miss even big things. Crowds are one area this happens. It's not that people don't see the mage disappear, it's that they are seeing everyone disappear and reappear all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the problem. You're assuming the HAB is just watching the crowd, not in the crowd, not right infront of the mage teleporting. For the purposes of HAB, you need to assume the Bystander could be from any single perspective, and that counts for the arrival location as well as the departed one.<br /> <br /> Running into a crowd and teleporting away may seem like simply losing track of them from the point of view of a guy sat on a bench people watching, but perhaps not the guy who suddenly sees an empty space right in front of them.<br /> <br /> This is the same reason why walking into an empty bar and closing the door behind you to teleport doesn't make it coincidental. Sure from the outside it the guy could just be somewhere in the bar, and if not they may have ran out back, but form the perspective of a bystander inside, a guy just straight up vanished.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T12:47:15-08:00","id":1017225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1017180#post1017180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's the problem. You're assuming the HAB is just watching the crowd, not in the crowd, not right infront of the mage teleporting. For the purposes of HAB, you need to assume the Bystander could be from any single perspective, and that counts for the arrival location as well as the departed one.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I am explicitly not assuming that. I've said that several times now. The entire second paragraph you quoted was all about how people <i>in the crowd</i> expect to see other people appear and disappear around them.<br /> <br /> As for the arrival location, I believe I already listed that as one of the reasons why coincidental crowd teleportation was not as trivial as you were assuming. You can do the same trick, but you need to have already made sure there is a suitable crowd where you are headed. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Running into a crowd and teleporting away may seem like simply losing track of them from the point of view of a guy sat on a bench people watching, but perhaps not the guy who suddenly sees an empty space right in front of them. </div> </div> </div>How long do you think someone moving in a crowd stays in your field of view? Without anyone getting between you or you looking away for a moment? How long do you think your eyes stay looking in any one direction if you aren't actively paying attention to something? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is the same reason why walking into an empty bar and closing the door behind you to teleport doesn't make it coincidental. Sure from the outside it the guy could just be somewhere in the bar, and if not they may have ran out back, but form the perspective of a bystander inside, a guy just straight up vanished. </div> </div> </div>The guy in the bar isn't expecting someone to brush past him and disappear, the guy in the crowd is. Actually, he's expecting hundreds of people to do that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T13:18:20-08:00","id":1017260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1017225#post1017225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I am explicitly not assuming that. I've said that several times now. The entire second paragraph you quoted was all about how people <i>in the crowd</i> expect to see other people appear and disappear around them.<br /> <br /> How long do you think someone moving in a crowd stays in your field of view? Without anyone getting between you or you looking away for a moment? How long do you think your eyes stay looking in any one direction if you aren't actively paying attention to something?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Have you never been in a slow moving crowd? You can end up staring at the same people for up to ten minutes. Even fast moving crowds, I'll notice and maybe even recognise people who are and have been moving around me. That guy with the Snoopy tie, that lady with hair a particular shade of brown, that person who's so obviously playing pokemon Go.<br /> <br /> Even if they brush past you, they'll still be teleporting in someone's field of view. And even if everyone is literally looking at the ground at they walk, it's still conceivable that one of them would look up and see their sudden lack of presence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1017225#post1017225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for the arrival location, I believe I already listed that as one of the reasons why coincidental crowd teleportation was not as trivial as you were assuming. You can do the same trick, but you need to have already made sure there is a suitable crowd where you are headed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so it isn't coincidental magic then. It's vulgar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1017225#post1017225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The guy in the bar isn't expecting someone to brush past him and disappear, the guy in the crowd is. Actually, he's expecting hundreds of people to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The guy in the bar isn't expecting anything because he doesn't exist. They're hypothetical, they carry no expectations outside of the zeitgeist, and the zeitgeist says people don't just vanish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 12-14-2016, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T13:35:09-08:00","id":1017272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1017161#post1017161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, chose a bad example with the soldier although I should point out that someone unfamiliar with guns is unlikely to know what the change in weight is between shots. If you empty their gun at that point, the example still holds.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;bad example&quot; doesn't address the fundamental question of where in the books it says that an atypical witness changes vulgarity (as opposed to being able to spot a vulgar effect others would miss). They only possible case for this is in judging the difficulty of the Blatancy Ability. It's the only place where the knowledge base of the people seeing you do stuff directly matters. An Explainable Blatancy Effect could be an Absurd Blatancy Effect to a different crowd.<br /> <br /> And, even in this case, they atypical person isn't changing the default vulgarity of the spell, they're stopping you from hiding it well enough to get it by as coincidental.<br /> <br /> If something would be coincidental without Blatancy, no atypical witness matters to coincidental vs. vulgar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When a sleeper sees something that doesn't add up, there are two paths they can go: they can assume that their senses are wrong or they can assume that reality is. </div> </div> </div>That's not how this works. If a Sleeper sees something that doesn't add up, it's vulgar. It doesn't matter how they rationalize or cope with what they see. Once it is, &quot;this doesn't add up,&quot; in their brains, it's already vulgar. That's why props and staging can help make effects coincidental: they stop the HAP from failing to add things up. The &quot;movie set&quot; props to explain how someone got shot and shoot back up works because it adds up to the average perception. Not because there's an assumption that their senses were wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Our senses do not provide a perfect picture of the world. </div> </div> </div>By this slippery slope of bad logic, everything is coincidental unless the book says something is explicitly vulgar, because the HAP will always just rationalize what they see as a fault in their perceptions based on the imperfection of human senses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If teleportation is visually indistinguishable from stealth, why wouldn't it get the same benefit? </div> </div> </div>The same reason the Blatancy Ability has limits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The fact that people would grab for the latter over the former is precisely why blending into a crowd works as a coincidental </div> </div> </div>No. That's why you could get away with it being vulgar without witnesses even in a crowd.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1017225#post1017225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I am explicitly not assuming that. I've said that several times now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you need to explain it better. Because no matter how frequently say you're not assuming that, your arguments only make sense with that as an underlying assumption.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How long do you think someone moving in a crowd stays in your field of view? Without anyone getting between you or you looking away for a moment? How long do you think your eyes stay looking in any one direction if you aren't actively paying attention to something? </div> </div> </div>None of that matters to the HAP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The guy in the bar isn't expecting someone to brush past him and disappear, the guy in the crowd is. Actually, he's expecting hundreds of people to do that. </div> </div> </div>The guy in the crowd isn't expecting someone to brush past him and literally disappear. They're expecting to brush past him and not pay any more attention to him. This is a difference you continue to ignore.<br /> <br /> Your saying that people in a crowd expect that the second they lose sight of something, they would find it sane and logical that the person they just brushed past can travel 100 miles away instantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T20:29:44-08:00","id":1017465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1017260#post1017260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you never been in a slow moving crowd? You can end up staring at the same people for up to ten minutes. Even fast moving crowds, I'll notice and maybe even recognise people who are and have been moving around me. That guy with the Snoopy tie, that lady with hair a particular shade of brown, that person who's so obviously playing pokemon Go.<br /> <br /> Even if they brush past you, they'll still be teleporting in someone's field of view. And even if everyone is literally looking at the ground at they walk, it's still conceivable that one of them would look up and see their sudden lack of presence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you realize this, but your entire example actually feeds into my point. In all your talk of noticing the people around you, you are describing their identifiable features, not when they moved in and out of your perception. You were losing track of them all along. There were plenty of them that disappeared and you never saw them again. For most of them you couldn't possibly tell me if they disappeared to your right, to your left, or just vanished. <br /> <br /> This is the part that messes everyone up. Most of what you think you are seeing right now, you aren't actually seeing. At any moment you are taking in a very small fraction of that image and your brain is filling in the rest from it's memory of what you looked at in the last few seconds. Sometimes that information is wrong. In an empty room this doesn't matter so much because your eyes are automatically drawn towards sudden movements and your peripheral vision can catch those. In a crowd there are too many sudden movements to deal with them all, so you miss things. People can easily (and unintentionally) move out of your view as your eyes map another part of the scene, leaving an empty spot when your eyes return a few tenths of a second later. You don't notice because you are so used to making adjustments to compensate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ah, so it isn't coincidental magic then. It's vulgar. </div> </div> </div>If you teleport into a mostly empty location, yeah. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The guy in the bar isn't expecting anything because he doesn't exist. They're hypothetical, they carry no expectations outside of the zeitgeist, and the zeitgeist says people don't just vanish. </div> </div> </div>The zeitgeist also says people easily disappear in crowds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1017272#post1017272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The &quot;bad example&quot; doesn't address the fundamental question of where in the books it says that an atypical witness changes vulgarity (as opposed to being able to spot a vulgar effect others would miss). They only possible case for this is in judging the difficulty of the Blatancy Ability. It's the only place where the knowledge base of the people seeing you do stuff directly matters. An Explainable Blatancy Effect could be an Absurd Blatancy Effect to a different crowd.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a feeling we are talking past each other on this one, so lets set it aside for now. I'll give you my approach on it later if we can reconcile the rest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's not how this works. If a Sleeper sees something that doesn't add up, it's vulgar. It doesn't matter how they rationalize or cope with what they see. Once it is, &quot;this doesn't add up,&quot; in their brains, it's already vulgar. That's why props and staging can help make effects coincidental: they stop the HAP from failing to add things up. The &quot;movie set&quot; props to explain how someone got shot and shoot back up works because it adds up to the average perception. Not because there's an assumption that their senses were wrong. </div> </div> </div>I think we are saying the same thing here. Certain events and props can provide a convenient explanation for sleepers so they don't have to face the impossible. If those things are present, what would be vulgar is instead coincidental. For effects like disappearing, smoke bombs, strobe lights, and things that disorient or otherwise make people doubt their own senses count as that kind of prop. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By this slippery slope of bad logic, everything is coincidental unless the book says something is explicitly vulgar, because the HAP will always just rationalize what they see as a fault in their perceptions based on the imperfection of human senses. </div> </div> </div>Not really. Our senses are very good, but they do let us down in specific ways in specific circumstances. Crowds happen to be one of those circumstances for motion tracking and edge detection. They won't hide a fireball, or even a strange looking human. And something you could easily miss in the bustle of a crowd becomes blindingly obvious in, say, a meeting room.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then you need to explain it better. Because no matter how frequently say you're not assuming that, your arguments only make sense with that as an underlying assumption. </div> </div> </div>Probably true, vision is really strange and more than a little counterintuitive. I would say you should probably try to forget those assumptions though, because I think they are actively getting in the way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> None of that matters to the HAP. </div> </div> </div>It matters because of how vision works. The only way the hypothetical observer wouldn't have the same problems a regular crowd goer would is if he was actively focusing his attention on the Mage, and I find that level of intensity to be a tedious interpretation of the principle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your saying that people in a crowd expect that the second they lose sight of something, they would find it sane and logical that the person they just brushed past can travel 100 miles away instantly. </div> </div> </div>Are you sure you aren't arguing HOP? Because there's no reasonable viewpoint an average person could be in that he could see that. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T21:00:41-08:00","id":1017476,"title":"","content":"Ok, one last time and then I'm done.<br /> <br /> HAB DOES NOT CARE IF ANYONE NOTICED YOU.<br /> <br /> IT ONLY CARES IF WHAT YOU'RE DOING IS EXPLAINABLE.<br /> <br /> If you teleport out in the open, that cannot be explained, it just cannot. It doesn't matter if you're diving into a crowd or a swimming pool. If someone was watching you intently and you suddenly vanished, and try Know that you vanished, then it's vulgar with witnesses. Otherwise it's just Vulgar.<br /> <br /> If you are in an empty room and you Corr 3 out, it's vulgar. That much we agree.<br /> <br /> If you are in an room with three other people and Corr 3 out, it's vulgar with witnesses. If none of them are looking at you, then it's just vulgar. I assume you agree with this too.<br /> <br /> How about 10 people? Vulgar with witnesses unless none of them look at you, them it's vulgar. However there are now 10 pairs of eyes, so the likelihood of being seen is even greater.<br /> <br /> How about 20 people? Why should it change? More people greater chance to be seen.<br /> <br /> How many people does it take for it to become coincidental?<br /> <br /> None, that's not how HAB works. It's not about human perception, it's not about cocentration, and it's certainly has nothing to do with distraction.<br /> <br /> It's simply saying &quot;if someone saw me teleport, would they think it's normal?&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not &quot;do they notice me teleport&quot; it's not &quot;would they even register a teleporting to have occurred&quot; and it's not at all &quot;would they mistake my teleporting away as getting lost in the crowd&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's just &quot;if someone was staring at me, standing right behind me, eyes glued to my head and walking to stay exactly 5 cm behind me at all times, and I suddenly teleported away, would that be normal to them?&quot;<br /> <br /> That answer must be No.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Optical illusions are not enough to back out of HAB.<br /> Limited attention is not enough to back out of HAB.<br /> Being the equivilant of a face in a see of faces of hiding in plain sight is not enough to back out of HAB.<br /> <br /> The HAB has seen you. They can't see what's in your pockets, what's hidden under your hat, what's in your mouth, how badly you're hurt, or what you're thinking. If it did then it Would be HOO.<br /> But HAB can't see all that stuff. HAB only sees you. It's sees you no matter where you are, no matter how hard you are to see, no matter how difficult it is to take in all this sense data.<br /> <br /> HAB sees you. It always sees you. That's what is so Hypothetical about this Hypotheitcal Average Bystander. We first assume you have been seen by them.<br /> <br /> There. I've laboured the point to death.<br /> <br /> Goodnight everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T21:47:14-08:00","id":1017491,"title":"","content":"This thread has helped me understand what I think of when I think of the Hypothetical Average Perceiver. To some extent without realizing it I was ignoring the fact the HAP isn't just in the area looking around, they're actually perceiving the actual location of the magic. But what that means can vary. Most people would agree that you can conjure something in your pocket Coincidentally under the gaze of the HAP, that the HAP isn't perceiving the inside of your pocket even though that's where the Effect is happening. Similarly the average person who is close enough to someone in a crowd to see him--if the crowd is sufficiently dense and active<i>--</i>is much more likely to be occluding the mage than perceiving him. In specific circumstances--with high numbers, lots of overall distraction, good stealth rolls, and a geographical location where the bar for Coincidence happens to be lower, it would be possible to teleport... maybe further along in the same crowd.<br /> <br /> Because the HAP perceives the <i>Effect</i> and not the subject of the Effect, the HAP should follow the subject to the new location. If the surroundings are completely different then it's Vulgar. This tends to limit the range. There are--I think--reasonable kludges that help limit teleportation further. We acknowledge even under a mostly HAP system that there are things that are inherently, objectively Vulgar such as crossing the Gauntlet or healing Aggravated damage. One could decree that you can't Coincidentally teleport farther than you could travel by foot in half an hour,* say, unless you're doing something like traveling to the kind of Al-i-Batin meta-maze mentioned earlier. In that case it would have to be a temporary Effect that would reverse before you could possibly leave the chamber or the chamber would have to be inescapable (without more Correspondence Effects) at the other end. By setting these conditions ahead of time, retroactive Vulgarity no longer becomes necessary.<br /> <br /> Admittedly this is mashing together several heterogynous ideas to arrive at circumstances where teleporting coincidentally (particularly in crowds since that's where the conversation went) is sometimes Coincidental but not reliably so and not a free pass to go wherever you want to go. To me, that is fine. Trying to use perfectly objective and consistent rules for something inherently subjective doesn't make sense to me. I place more stock in <i>intuitive </i>coherence. And I'm with Saiku in one sense, the ultimate goal is gameplay. That means balancing the need to limit characters with the need to let them do cool stuff.<br /> <br /> *Here you're using a bit of HOP as a kludge, by taking the perspective of the whole world into account. Or, looked at another way, envisioning the HAP seeing the person on live television a few minutes after running into them in person. The distance would have to be somewhat plausible by that test.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","user":"Faradn","date":". 12-15-2016, 01:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T05:52:48-08:00","id":1017609,"title":"","content":"I disagree especially with one point @Saikou<br /> The \u201cwe assume the HAB perceives us\u201c.<br /> That would be a Hypothetical Average Perceiver.<br /> The Bystander being Average isn't expected to know all, see all or even just exceptional or extraordinary good.<br /> I can easily see a HAB miss someone disappear in a crowd and reemerge in a crowd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T05:58:58-08:00","id":1017611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1017609#post1017609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree especially with one point @Saikou<br /> The \u201cwe assume the HAB perceives us\u201c.<br /> That would be a Hypothetical Average Perceiver.<br /> The Bystander being Average isn't expected to know all, see all or even just exceptional or extraordinary good.<br /> I can easily see a HAB miss someone disappear in a crowd and reemerge in a crowd.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting point. But I'd say this is more semantics than anything else, because I'm using HAB and HAP interchangeably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T06:41:16-08:00","id":1017621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence?p=1017476#post1017476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, one last time and then I'm done.<br /> <br /> HAB DOES NOT CARE IF ANYONE NOTICED YOU.<br /> <br /> IT ONLY CARES IF WHAT YOU'RE DOING IS EXPLAINABLE.</div> </div> </div> </div>No need for all caps, we agree on this point, the only thing that seems to be at issue is what constitutes 'explainable'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you teleport out in the open, that cannot be explained, it just cannot. It doesn't matter if you're diving into a crowd or a swimming pool. If someone was watching you intently and you suddenly vanished, and try Know that you vanished, then it's vulgar with witnesses. Otherwise it's just Vulgar.<br /> <br /> If you are in an empty room and you Corr 3 out, it's vulgar. That much we agree.<br /> <br /> If you are in an room with three other people and Corr 3 out, it's vulgar with witnesses. If none of them are looking at you, then it's just vulgar. I assume you agree with this too.<br /> <br /> How about 10 people? Vulgar with witnesses unless none of them look at you, them it's vulgar. However there are now 10 pairs of eyes, so the likelihood of being seen is even greater.<br /> <br /> How about 20 people? Why should it change? More people greater chance to be seen.<br /> <br /> How many people does it take for it to become coincidental? </div> </div> </div>Bypassing a discussion about the paradox of the heaps for the moment...<br /> <br /> It happens at the threshold, wherever that is, where the mundane explanation is significantly easier than the crazy one. We know that can happen, we have examples of props that make provide convenient explanations and foci that don't technically fit within the modern paradigm but are close enough that no one cares. If people have a decent reason to think that what they see is normal, the effect is coincidental.<br /> <br /> Now, as far as I am concerned, in HAP the mere fact that people can easily disappear in crowds is enough reason to meet that requirement. HAP already puts largely arbitrary restrictions on the observer in the name of intuition and fun, what's one more when you have a good trope for it? It is only HOP that requires getting into details about the nature of vision, how people disappear in front of you all the time, and how there is no such thing as 'happening to be looking in the right direction at the right time.' But either way you handle it, people in crowds have significant reasons to think that specific visual oddities, like vanishing, are mundane occurrences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> None, that's not how HAB works. It's not about human perception, it's not about cocentration, and it's certainly has nothing to do with distraction.<br /> <br /> It's simply saying &quot;if someone saw me teleport, would they think it's normal?&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not &quot;do they notice me teleport&quot; it's not &quot;would they even register a teleporting to have occurred&quot; and it's not at all &quot;would they mistake my teleporting away as getting lost in the crowd&quot;. </div> </div> </div>I'll say it once more. It isn't that they don't see you vanish. They see you vanish. They see lots of people vanish. All the time. Your trick doesn't stand out. It's not unusual.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's just &quot;if someone was staring at me, standing right behind me, eyes glued to my head and walking to stay exactly 5 cm behind me at all times, and I suddenly teleported away, would that be normal to them?&quot;<br /> <br /> That answer must be No. </div> </div> </div>Sure, that answer in that case is no. But at what point did the hypothetical observer develop an obsession with the back of your head? I don't even do that in HOP, I save that kind of thing for particularly aggressive reality zones like Technocratic Labs. If you have to ascribe that level of intensity to the hypothetical observer to get them to notice the effect, chances are it was a coincidental.<br /> <br /> I think we are starting to narrow in on the problem here. I'm not going to say it's not a valid way of interpreting the rules, but it is a very hardline stance that runs contrary to the spirit of HAP.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Optical illusions are not enough to back out of HAB.<br /> Limited attention is not enough to back out of HAB.<br /> Being the equivilant of a face in a see of faces of hiding in plain sight is not enough to back out of HAB. </div> </div> </div>By themselves no, those aren't enough. But if they are so common that people expect their senses to be unreliable, that matters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The HAB has seen you. They can't see what's in your pockets, what's hidden under your hat, what's in your mouth, how badly you're hurt, or what you're thinking. If it did then it Would be HOO.<br /> But HAB can't see all that stuff. HAB only sees you. It's sees you no matter where you are, no matter how hard you are to see, no matter how difficult it is to take in all this sense data.<br /> <br /> HAB sees you. It always sees you. That's what is so Hypothetical about this Hypotheitcal Average Bystander. We first assume you have been seen by them.<br /> <br /> There. I've laboured the point to death.<br /> <br /> Goodnight everyone. </div> </div> </div>Right, there's a lot I have to say about this, but it involves turning this into a HAP/HOP conversation (moreso than it is already, I mean). Is that okay?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}